BIT-12: Factor once, solve into the segments, keep coefficients and segment lists

For each dispersing pipe, species and step, the tridiagonal system was
factored three times for its three right-hand sides, the responses were
copied into the segments in three more list walks, the dispersion
coefficient was recomputed from unchanged hydraulics, and the segment list
was walked again after the nodal solve. Factor once, back-substitute
straight into the segments, keep each pipe's coefficient while its
hydraulics are unchanged, and keep the segment list between passes.

Requires: none
Results: identical (every concentration, the output file and the report are unchanged)

Apply from the root of an EPANET-MSX checkout at 85a303d, after FIX-01, FIX-02 and BIT-01 to BIT-11:
    git apply --whitespace=nowarn BIT-12.patch
or use tools/build-msx.sh, which applies the series in order.

